<title>USA: NOPA to issue weekly soybean crush on Fridays.</title>
<headline>NOPA to issue weekly soybean crush on Fridays.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Oilseed Processors Association said on Thursday that beginning on June 27, it will issue its weekly U.S. soybean crushings data on Fridays at 7 a.m. EDT (1100 GMT).</p>
<p>The report previously has been issued every Thursday at 4:30 p.m. EDT (2030 GMT).</p>
<p>NOPA also said its monthly soybean crushings data, which is usually released around the middle of every month, will be released at 7 a.m. EDT (1100 GMT) the day after its completion.</p>
<p>NOPA reported Thursday that 24.540 million bushels of soybeans were crushed in the week to June 18, compared with 25.378 million bushels the previous week.</p>
